    "# In my computational design modeling class, I am studying sidewalk sheds in New York City and the complexities surrounding them. While they are often criticized as a loophole that allows building owners to delay repairs, they have also unintentionally become an extension of public space for residents. As a next step, I want to explore their thermal qualities and potential to create comfort. At this stage, my goal is to identify and map neighborhoods with a high concentration of sidewalk sheds that have remained for more than five years.\n",
